with almost 500 sessions at next 2018  it's understandable that you couldn't  get to them all so if you didn't see CIC  D in a surveillance world then stay  tuned because here's the rewind the  development ecosystem is always changing  for companies as they look to grow and  scale their businesses continuous  integration and continuous delivery or  CIC D has become an essential process  for helping teams deliver code changes  more frequently and reliably thanks to  increases in serverless technology teams  can build and deploy their code with  even more speed and structure first  let's define what we mean by serverless  the core idea here is that we're able to  focus on running our application code  without having to worry about the  infrastructure or the underlying logic  used to run or scale our application  service options are increasing in  popularity and tools around these are  still evolving and growing rapidly in  fact Google has had a number of service  offerings going as far back as app  engine which released ten years ago all  of these cover a wide variety of  services but for CIC D will mainly be  focusing on compute offerings such as  App Engine or cloud functions so when  looking at CI CD there's a whole bunch  of things like build agents and  configuration management that we would  need to deal with in a legacy  environment instead of jumping through  hoops and managing the infrastructure  for all of these let's focus on  embracing serverless concepts and best  practices by doing this we can reduce  our overhead and spend more time on our  application service lets us focus on  making our deployments automatic faster  and safer by really drilling into the  automated tasks and process our code can  quickly go from commit to deployed and  we're able to customize build steps such  as testing and manual approval to  capture all the benefits of coding in a  surveillance world we can configure  tasks and deployment strategies as  needed such as blue green and canary for  all the processes we've just outlined we  need a tool to manage all the travelling  that our code needs to do and that's  where cloud build comes in this is a  pretty typical workflow and cloud build  hubs improve developer velocity and  manage the build steps like packaging  and testing deploying to staging and  reviewing it before finally promoting it  into production who cloud build is also  service and highly configurable with  built-in support for CLI tools  encryption for api secrets  and local build support whether building  on VMs or serverless a well-structured  CI CD pipeline lets us benefit from  automation cloud build helps us it  create the rules of the system and get  all the efficiencies without having to  worry about any of the details of the  infrastructure in the talk  Christopher Sanson takes us through a  demonstration of his new prepster shop  built on App Engine firebase and cloud  functions I definitely recommend  checking it out to see all the features  of cloud built in action and how it  really enables CI CD in a serverless  world if you'd like to see the full talk  check out the link in the description  below and don't forget to subscribe to  the cloud YouTube channel for more great  next rewind content thanks for watching  you  [Music]
 

